{title: Holy, Holy, Holy}
{artist: Reginald Heber, 1826; music John B. Dykes, 1861}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}
{copyright: Words and music: public domain. Chords © 2026 Simon Davy.}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! Lord God Al[D]mighty!
[D]Early in the [G]morning our [A]song shall [D]rise to Thee;
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! Mer[D]ciful and [A]mighty!
God in [D]three Per[G]sons, [A]blessed Trin[D]ity!

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! All the saints a[D]dore Thee,
[D]Casting down their [G]golden crowns a[A]round the glassy [D]sea;
[D]Cherubim and [G]seraphim [D]falling down be[A]fore Thee,
Who [D]wert, and [G]art, and [A]evermore shalt [D]be.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! Though the darkness [D]hide Thee,
[D]Though the eye of [G]sinful man Thy [A]glory may not [D]see;
[D]Only Thou art [G]holy; there [D]is none be[A]side Thee,
[D]Perfect in [G]power, in [A]love, and pu[D]rity.

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! Lord God Al[D]mighty!
[D]All Thy works shall [G]praise Thy name, in [A]earth and sky and [D]sea;
[D]Holy, holy, [G]holy! Mer[D]ciful and [A]mighty!
God in [D]three Per[G]sons, [A]blessed Trin[D]ity!
